Now the play program. AC'97 PCM-out DMA engine (PO) registers in NABM (BAR1, r1=0xc400) are based at offset 0x10:
- 0x10 PO_BDBAR (buffer descriptor list base address, 32-bit)
- 0x14 PO_CIV (current index, RO)
- 0x15 PO_LVI (last valid index)
- 0x16 PO_SR (status, 16-bit; bit0=DCH DMA halted, bit3=BCIS)
- 0x1B PO_CR (control, 8-bit; bit0=RPBM run, bit1=reset)

The BDL entry is 8 bytes: dword0 = buffer physical address, dword1 = low 16 bits = number of samples (16-bit words), bit31 = IOC, bit30 = BUP. r9 = bytes of PCM, so samples = r9/2. I'll build one BDL entry at r12 (scratch) pointing at r7.

